@startuml kanban-check-activity
' kanban-check — Activity diagram (associated process)
' Sources: process/kanban-check.md and process/kanban_check.sh
title kanban-check — deterministic read-only report

start
:Resolve operator\n(gh api user, unless the invoker names one);

:Step 0 — freshness and hygiene\n(git fetch origin main -q, git status,\ngit worktree list, extra branches);

:Read board conventions from origin/main\n(git show origin/main:AGENTS.md);

:Step 1 — pull state;
:Board fetch — live work only\n(gh project item-list --query -status:Done);
:Guard board fetch with totalCount\n(truncation is a hard failure);

:Issue fetch — deliberate superset\n(gh issue list --state all, plus bodies);
:Guard issue fetch by returned equals limit;\nrefetch once at double, else report LIMITS;

:PR fetch — gh pr list;
:Read HUMAN-REVIEW-QUEUE.md from origin/main;
:Resolve remote branches — git ls-remote --heads origin;

:Step 2 — sync findings\n(closed or merged not Done, PR without card,\nHRQ items without card, checked-off HRQ items,\nstale work claims);

:Step 3 — gate findings\n(closed human-review with no finalized marker;\nopen Awaiting-human-action with new comments);

:Step 4 — queue and candidates\n(operator gates with ask lines, Todo by number);

:Classify nothing — interpretation is the orchestrator's;\nquote gate payloads and candidate comments verbatim;

:Emit report between fixed markers\n=== KANBAN-CHECK REPORT === ... === END ===;

stop

note right
  READ-ONLY. No gh mutation, no repo file
  edit, and git is limited to the allowlist:
  fetch origin main -q, status, show,
  worktree list, branch, ls-remote.
end note

note right
  NON-RECURSIVE. Run every step yourself;
  never spawn another agent.
end note
@enduml
